{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Because he has despised the word of YHWH.</b> The entire Torah is included under the term 'the word of YHWH,' for since he worships idolatry intentionally, behold he despises the entire Torah in its totality." "<b>And it is possible</b> to interpret 'the word of YHWH' by way of the plain sense (peshat) as referring to the first utterance of the Ten Commandments — for he transgresses the commandment of 'I am' and despises the divinity; and 'he has broken His commandment' refers to the negative commandment of 'You shall not have' — which he violated and transgressed. The upshot of the matter is that he despised 'I am' and nullified 'You shall not have.'" "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'Because he has despised the word of YHWH' — this refers to one who shows contempt for the Torah and the heretic (apikoros). And our Rabbis of blessed memory learned here that a Torah scholar is called 'the word of YHWH,' because he declares the word of YHWH and justifies the multitudes, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 103): ״גבורי כח עשי דברו לשמוע בקול דברו״ — 'Mighty in strength, who do His word, to hearken to the voice of His word'; and the heretic who despises him, despises the word of YHWH."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:39.925731618Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}